WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:05.872
♪♪

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.874
-Here's how the game works.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:09.942
-Matthew and Johnny,
here you go.

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:11.510
Here's yours.
-There's yours.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.680
Matthew, for you. Johnny.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.880
-Johnny, there's yours.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.082
-Don't embarrass me.

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.583
-We'll try.
-This is national television.

00:00:17.583 --> 00:00:19.519
-It's hard not to.
-This is for you right here.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:20.954
-I'm going to read you
a question about your dad,

00:00:20.954 --> 00:00:23.856
and I want you to write down
what you think the answer is.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:25.291
Rob, you'll write down
the real answer.

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.292
-All right.
-Okay.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.460
Then, you'll reveal your answers

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.228
to see which son is really

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:31.797
the Best Son. Here we go.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:35.768
First question is, "If Rob
could only watch one movie

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:39.172
for the rest of his life,
what would it be?"

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.806
I'm not looking.
I want to be surprised.

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:42.608
[ Drums playing softly ]

00:00:42.608 --> 00:00:43.810
Don't look Matthew.
Don't look.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:44.978
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:47.012
-Was he peeking?
-Matthew was peeking, I think.

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:48.448
-So, he should...
-No, it's all right, we'll see.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:50.549
We'll see what happens.
Here we go.

00:00:50.549 --> 00:00:51.718
You ready?
Matthew, have you written it?

00:00:51.718 --> 00:00:53.386
-Yeah, yeah.
-All right, here we go.

00:00:53.386 --> 00:00:55.822
Matthew, reveal,
what movie would it be?

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:58.124
[ Drumroll]
"Goodfellas."

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:01.427
Very interesting, okay.
John Owen?

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:02.796
"Goodfellas"?

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:03.896
Rob Lowe?

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:05.531
[ Loud drumroll ]

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:06.832
Wow!

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:12.004
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Music plays ]

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:14.274
[ As Ray Liotta ] Karen!
-Karen!

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.541
Karen!
-You know what kind of people

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:18.144
go to j-- [ laughs ]
-That's the best.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:19.612
-Best movie.
-I think we watched that

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:20.713
when we were probably
a little too young.

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:22.081
-Yeah.
-All right, yeah yeah yeah.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:24.484
Let's not get into details
about when you watched that.

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:25.618
That's great.
I love that movie.

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.752
-Best movie ever!
-It's so good.

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:28.988
-All right, next question is,

00:01:28.988 --> 00:01:31.323
"If a genie gave Rob one wish,

00:01:31.323 --> 00:01:34.093
what would he wish for?"

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:35.962
-Johnny's laughing.
[ Drums playing softly ]

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:38.131
He's laughing.
He already is writing something.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.799
Matthew's stumped.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.800
He's not sure what it is.
-One wish?

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:44.537
-"If a genie gave Rob one wish,
what would he wish for?"

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.372
[ Drums playing softly ]

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:49.108
-That's so esoteric!

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:51.311
-Hey man, it's 2017.
-Okay, um...

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:54.713
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.713 --> 00:01:56.782
-Genies give one wish now.

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:58.451
[ Drums playing softly ]

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.119
All right, here we go.
Everyone's still writing.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.520
No drawing pictures, either.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.323
Ready?
Matthew, still writing.

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:05.824
What did you write down?

00:02:05.824 --> 00:02:06.826
-"Live to be 100."
[ Drumroll ]

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:08.328
-"Live to be 100!"

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:10.163
Interesting.

00:02:10.163 --> 00:02:11.931
What did you say, Johnny?
-"More wishes."

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.766
-Ah, "More wishes!"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:15.067
That's a good secret one.

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:17.903
-I'm going with Matthew Lowe,
"Eternal life"!

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:19.438
-Wow, "Eternal life"!

00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:21.507
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Music plays ]

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:26.479
Matthew, eternal life!
[ Laughs ]

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.181
-I should --
But John Owen's smarter

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.449
than all of us,
and he picks the one

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:30.816
you should pick.
-That's like cheating, though.

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:32.451
-Maybe the loophole wasn't
the way to go.

00:02:32.451 --> 00:02:34.253
-Yeah, but it's good!
-No, you went with the loophole.

00:02:34.253 --> 00:02:36.355
What were you about to...
-I was going to say --

00:02:36.355 --> 00:02:38.791
I questioned it at first.
I thought maybe this is immoral,

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.960
but I think that it's allowed.
-Matthew's in the lead.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.861
Matthew's in the lead
for being Best Son.

00:02:42.861 --> 00:02:44.631
Here we go.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.198
-Damn it!

00:02:46.198 --> 00:02:47.500
-Next question.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:50.203
"What makes Rob laugh
the hardest?"

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.705
[ Laughter ]

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.474
[ Laughing ] "What makes
Rob laugh the hardest?"

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.708
All right, guys.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.243
[ Drums playing softly ]

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:58.911
What makes Dad laugh
the hardest?

00:02:58.911 --> 00:02:59.946
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.014
-Like, think more of a giggle,

00:03:02.014 --> 00:03:03.983
closer to a guffaw, maybe.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.117
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.117 --> 00:03:06.652
-I don't think he even knows.

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:09.388
-Like a... [ laughs ]

00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:11.891
That type of fun laugh where...
-Uh...

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:13.993
...it's, like, out-of-breath
laughing like, "Wow."

00:03:13.993 --> 00:03:16.863
-Okay.
-Crying, tears are coming out.

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.531
-Like, "That makes me laugh
so hard, oh, man.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.865
That was really funny."

00:03:19.865 --> 00:03:23.402
Could be a comedy,
could be something physical,

00:03:23.402 --> 00:03:26.973
could be an impression,
could be anything, really.

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:29.108
Matthew, you're good?
-Yeah, I think.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:30.542
We'll see.
-All right, that's good.

00:03:30.542 --> 00:03:32.078
Matthew, don't look
at your brother's thing!

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.178
-I'm already done.

00:03:33.178 --> 00:03:35.047
-All right.
-Is he cheating?

00:03:35.047 --> 00:03:36.381
-All right, ready?
Here we go.

00:03:36.381 --> 00:03:38.717
Matthew, what did
you write down?

00:03:38.717 --> 00:03:40.219
-"Funny animals."
-"Funny animals"!

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:42.021
-He's going the safe route.
-Okay, "Funny animals."

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.022
[ Drumroll ]

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.757
-"My friends."

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.193
-Your friends?
-Yeah.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:48.527
He's always laughing
at my friends.

00:03:48.527 --> 00:03:51.264
-I do, that is true.
-His friends are funny?

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:52.297
Okay, but what did you say?

00:03:52.297 --> 00:03:53.899
Is it not his friends?

00:03:53.899 --> 00:03:56.502
[ Loud drumroll ]

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.238
-Doctor --
Okay, but I showed you that

00:03:58.238 --> 00:03:59.938
so I should maybe get
a point for this.

00:03:59.938 --> 00:04:01.174
-"Steve Brule"?
-Steve Brule!

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:03.442
Are we talking about John...
-Right?

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:05.077
-I showed how funny he is.
-Dead silence in the audience.

00:04:05.077 --> 00:04:06.278
-John C. Reilly...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.278 --> 00:04:08.580
-Dead silence.
Everyone like, "We don't know

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:10.015
John C. Reilly."
-John C. Reilly is

00:04:10.015 --> 00:04:11.617
Dr. Steve Brule.
-The best thing ever.

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:12.718
-It might be one of
the funniest things

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:13.986
I've ever seen.
-I'm not crazy, right?

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:15.454
-Yeah, Tim and Eric.
Yeah, absolutely it's great.

00:04:15.454 --> 00:04:16.488
-Yes.
-Okay, good, all right.

00:04:16.488 --> 00:04:18.357
-But in fairness,
who showed you that?

00:04:18.357 --> 00:04:19.391
-They turned me onto it.

00:04:19.391 --> 00:04:20.993
-Well, they?
-They're my barometers

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.127
of anything that's actually...
-Who in particular showed you?

00:04:22.127 --> 00:04:24.396
-Which one specifically?
-Matthew and Johnny.

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:25.998
-No, it was me!

00:04:25.998 --> 00:04:27.533
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.469
-That's shady.
-Yeah, it's a little shady.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:31.837
But we talked to the judge,
and we're going to give Johnny

00:04:31.837 --> 00:04:33.506
one point for that,
so it's a tie game.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.708
-Yay!
[ Music plays ]

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:38.110
-This is the last --
the last question.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:39.612
-All right.
-The last question.

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:41.814
This is to see
who is the Best Son.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.383
This is worth 1,000 points.

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:45.584
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.584 --> 00:04:47.587
-1,000?
-This one's worth 1,000 points.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.421
-Worth 1,000?
-Whoever wins this one wins.

00:04:49.421 --> 00:04:50.656
-Well, do you want to
try for it, too?

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:52.858
-I -- Yeah, I'll guess.
-Yeah, get in on this.

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:53.893
-I'll get in on this one.

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.961
-Get in on this.
I mean, this is just

00:04:55.961 --> 00:04:57.496
riveting stuff.
You've gotta be --

00:04:57.496 --> 00:04:59.065
-If you win, we're kicked out
of our house, though.

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.133
-That's the problem.
-Last question.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:04.370
"What is Rob's hidden talent
that not too many people

00:05:04.370 --> 00:05:06.272
know about?"
-Ooh!

00:05:06.272 --> 00:05:11.444
[ Soft drum plays ]

00:05:11.444 --> 00:05:14.180
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:20.353
-And you can't say --
We all know he's a great actor.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:21.854
Can you sing?
I forget if you can sing.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.557
Maybe you're very athletic?

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:26.859
No, I feel like maybe there's
and artsy -- You know what?

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:28.194
I'm just going to take
a wild guess.

00:05:28.194 --> 00:05:31.063
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.063 --> 00:05:33.032
All right, here we go.

00:05:33.032 --> 00:05:35.835
Uh, Matthew?

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:36.935
[ Drumroll ]
Wait, "Impressions"?

00:05:36.935 --> 00:05:38.404
I was going to say impressions!

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:39.471
-That's a good one, damn it.

00:05:39.471 --> 00:05:40.973
-Johnny?

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:42.508
"History buff"!

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:44.877
-He knows his history.
-Rob Lowe?

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.078
-Surfing!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.078 --> 00:05:47.880
-They're all good!

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.048
-I was going to say impressions,

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.716
too, 'cause he is
a great impressionist.

00:05:50.716 --> 00:05:51.817
I thought maybe you paint.

00:05:51.817 --> 00:05:53.252
Do you paint?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.354
[ Music plays ]
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:57.156
Do you paint?
-I don't paint.

00:05:57.156 --> 00:05:58.323
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:58.323 --> 00:06:00.392
You're such a loser!
Why don't you paint?

00:06:00.392 --> 00:06:01.393
-What are you good at?

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:03.495
-Guys, we have a tie.

00:06:03.495 --> 00:06:05.198
You're both the Best Son.
-Aww!

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:07.533
I like that.
I love the way that works out.

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:08.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Music plays ]

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:11.470
-Matthew and John Owen Lowe,
everybody!

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:12.872
Check out "The Lowe Files"
on the A&amp;E!

